# Kovobot environment variables (example)
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env. In production, keep secrets in
# Google Secret Manager and expose them to Cloud Run as these variables.
#
# loadConfig in packages/config reads the server's settings. The rest belong to
# features docs/design.md describes that aren't built yet. Names follow each
# vendor's own SDK convention where one exists.
#
# Tags: [hosted] = needed only in the hosted service. [self-hosted] = only when
# self-hosting. Untagged = both.
#
# The server starts with an empty environment (self-hosted, local defaults).
# To self-host, follow SELF-HOSTING.md: docker compose up -d needs only one Model
# provider key here. On a server, also set KOVOBOT_URL, SESSION_SECRET,
# SIGN_UP_OPEN=false and SMTP so sign-in links are emailed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# hosted | self-hosted. One switch that sets safe defaults together:
# self-hosted turns billing, Plan limits and analytics off and allows local (stdio) MCP servers.
KOVOBOT_MODE=self-hosted
NODE_ENV=development

# Public URLs. Stripe and Telegram webhooks and MCP OAuth callbacks are built from API_URL.
# Deployed, the API serves the web app, so both are the same https origin. In
# development Vite (5173) forwards /api to the API (3000).
APP_URL=http://localhost:5173
API_URL=http://localhost:3000
# [self-hosted] With docker compose up: the address people open Kovobot at. It sets
# both URLs above for the container. Defaults to http://localhost:8080; on a server,
# your https address (SELF-HOSTING.md).
# KOVOBOT_URL=
# The API's port. Cloud Run sets it.
# PORT=3000
# Whether new Customers can sign up. Open when self-hosted; when hosted it stays
# closed until launch, while the landing page collects a waitlist. At launch set
# it to true, deploy, then run pnpm leads:announce.
# SIGN_UP_OPEN=
# [hosted] The landing page's origin (GitHub Pages), allowed to post leads to the API.
# LANDING_URL=https://kovobot.com
# Set in the container image: the web app's build, served by the API.
# WEB_DIST_DIR=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database: Postgres holds the ledger, background jobs and sessions
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The local Postgres from docker-compose.yml (pnpm db:up). Tests create their own
# database on the same server, or on TEST_DATABASE_URL if set.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://kovobot:kovobot@localhost:54329/kovobot

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server secrets. Generate each with: openssl rand -base64 32
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signs session cookies. At least 32 characters. Required when hosted; self-hosted
# without it uses a temporary one, so everyone is signed out on restart.
SESSION_SECRET=
# Encrypts stored secrets: Customers' Own keys and their Channel app tokens.
# Rotating it needs a re-encryption job, so keep it stable.
SECRETS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model providers: our keys, used for hosted AI use paid from Credit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Self-hosted: the operator's own keys. Leave a Model provider blank to switch it off.
# Own keys that Customers add to a Bot live encrypted in the database, not here.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
XAI_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# [self-hosted] Optional local OpenAI-compatible server (Ollama, vLLM), e.g.
# http://localhost:11434/v1. The hosted service never calls a Customer-supplied URL.
OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_BASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Billing [hosted]: Stripe is the only payment rail
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both follow KOVOBOT_MODE (on when hosted, off when self-hosted), so a
# self-hosted install never charges. Set them only to override, e.g. a hosted
# staging install with billing off.
# BILLING_ENABLED=
# PLAN_LIMITS_ENABLED=
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Price IDs of the monthly Subscriptions: Pro ($20) and Max ($200).
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=
STRIPE_PRICE_MAX=
# Price ID of the one-time $1 Starter payment that unlocks Starter credit.
STRIPE_PRICE_STARTER=
# Stripe Tax is switched on in the Stripe dashboard and needs no variable.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web app and desktop app: public values, bundled into the client by Vite
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The web app calls the API on its own origin under /api, so it needs no API URL.
# The landing page (apps/landing) is a separate static site: its waitlist form
# posts to VITE_APP_URL, set at build time (the GitHub variable APP_URL in CI).
# Blank in development, where Vite forwards /api to the local API.
VITE_APP_URL=
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# [hosted] PostHog project key for browser analytics (public, write-only).
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sign-in: a one-time link by email, or Sign in with Google. No passwords.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google OAuth client for "Sign in with Google". Blank turns it off; set both or neither.
# Redirect URI to register with Google: API_URL + /api/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email: sign-in links, plus [hosted] invites, Credit warnings and failed
# Auto top-up notices
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider not chosen yet; any SMTP service works. Required when hosted.
# Self-hosted without SMTP_HOST writes sign-in links to the server log instead.
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASSWORD=
EMAIL_FROM="Kovobot <noreply@example.com>"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phone verification [hosted]: Starter credit is once per verified phone number
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Twilio Verify sends and checks the one-time code.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Connected apps: Composio, alongside MCP (ADR 0010)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hosted: our key. Self-hosted: optional, the operator's own key; blank means MCP only.
# Customers' app tokens stay with Composio, scoped to each Customer.
COMPOSIO_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analytics [hosted]: PostHog US cloud, content-free events only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ignored when KOVOBOT_MODE=self-hosted.
POSTHOG_API_KEY=
POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Channels: nothing to set here
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Each Customer registers its own Telegram, Discord and Slack app (ADR 0007)
# and enters its tokens on our website. They are stored encrypted with
# SECRETS_ENCRYPTION_KEY, and Telegram webhooks are registered under API_URL.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Computer service: a separate service whose only client is the Bot service (ADR 0001)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMPUTER_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:3100
# Shared secret the Bot service presents to the Computer service.
COMPUTER_SERVICE_API_KEY=
# Signs the short-lived tokens bound to one Computer (its Computer agent and live view).
# A Computer never holds Own keys or our Model provider keys.
COMPUTER_TOKEN_SIGNING_KEY=
# Follows KOVOBOT_MODE: docker when self-hosted (Linux only), cloud when hosted.
# Set only to override.
# COMPUTER_BACKEND=
# [self-hosted] Docker engine address. Blank uses the local socket.
DOCKER_HOST=

# Linux Computers [hosted]: Google Cloud, in the one US region that holds all data.
GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=
GCP_REGION=us-central1
GCP_ZONE=us-central1-a
# Local runs only. On Cloud Run, the service's attached service account is used.
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=

# Windows and macOS Computers [hosted]: AWS.
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# Local runs only. In production, assume a role instead of using long-lived keys.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS Managed Microsoft AD directory, required for the Remote Desktop user
# licences (one per Bot that operates a Windows Computer and per person who watches).
AWS_DIRECTORY_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Later: in docs/design.md but not used at launch. Leave blank until built.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Honcho: long-term memory beyond each Bot's notes.
HONCHO_API_KEY=
# AgentMail: an email inbox of each Bot's own. Inbound mail arrives under API_URL.
AGENTMAIL_API_KEY=
# AgentPhone: phone numbers, SMS, calls and iMessage lines, each subject to its Channel review.
AGENTPHONE_API_KEY=
